:: Werewolf First Encounter [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
Crickets chirp idly as fireflies dance around the moonlight forest. The air is calm and relaxing, cool without being cold, quiet without being silent. As the sun goes down, nature seems to take over and display just as much light and life as the day as you take a seat on a large rock to just take in the sights and sounds. You should probably think about heading home soon, the entire town already dark and beginning to settle down for the night, but figure one more minute wouldn’t hurt. <br>
<<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
<<needChange "Fun" 10>>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: BlueViolet">Then something pricks the back of your neck, causes your tail and ears to stand up on end.</span> Something need inside you, some primal instinct or hidden force claws at the back of your mind telling you one terrifying thing: <span style="Color: LightCoral">You are in danger.</span> <br>
<br>
Your head snaps to the bush as soon as it rustles, your heart skipping a beat as you stare into the darkness behind the leaves. <span style="Color: LightCoral">Then you see two, crimson red eyes peering at you. They glow in the dark, malice and hunger clear in their ruby glare. You slowly take a step back, so afraid you can hardly move. Then suddenly burst into a full run! <br>
<br>
You hear a loud rustle followed by quick, beast-like footsteps and a deep, low growl! You feel a sense of danger in your spine and turn left just in time to dodge the creature’s lunging strike, sending him colliding into a tree.</span> <span style="Color: BlueViolet">You turn your head as you run to get a glimpse at the creature, seeing a mass of fur and claws that seems like a mixture of man and wolf. You’ve seen something like this before in movies and cartoons, but they can’t be real… right? Werewolves don’t exist!</span> <br>
<br>
You nearly collide with a tree as you look back forward just in time. <span style="Color: Yellow">The creature will be on you again as soon as it recovers. With it’s speed, there is no chance you’ll be able to outrun it! You have to think of a plan, fast!</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Climb up a tree<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Thinking fast, you begin to scramble up the nearby tree as fast as you can. Your hope is that you can get up there and hide before it sees you or, at least, be out of the creature’s reach. While the tree isn’t super easy to climb, your adrenaline and fear drive you forward until- <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightCoral">CRASH! <br>
        <br>
        The creature is below you, clawing at the tree and grabbing for your legs! You scream, continuing to climb up in a terrified scramble until the branch you are holding onto crack… <br>
        <br>
        Time seems to move in slow motion as you fall, sure to die from the impact or from the creature’s maw. Is this really how your life ends?</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">But, before you can hit the ground, you feel something warm and furry catch you and drop you onto the ground safely.</span> <br>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Werewolf First Encounter 2]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Hide in the bushes<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Thinking fast, you dive into the nearest, biggest bush you can find. While not the best hiding spot, it’s all you have. You hope that the creature will think you kept running and leave so you can find a better chance to escape. Or, maybe, leave you alone until morning when you might be able to get help. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightCoral">CRACK! <br>
        <br>
        The creature steps on a branch as it approaches, causing your entire body to tense up. You put your hands over your mouth, too scared to even breath, and wait in fear for the creature to leave… <br>
        <br>
        Suddenly, a claw rips through the bushes and grabs at your legs! You scream, kicking and flailing about as you are yanked out of the bush! This is it, this is how you die! Eaten by some werewolf! You cover your eyes and feel as you are lifted off the ground and held aloft!</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: Yellow">But you are then dropped to the ground safely.</span> <br>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Werewolf First Encounter 2]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>

:: Werewolf First Encounter 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You open your eyes slowly and tremble at what you see. <span style="Color: BlueViolet">The creature, the werewolf, stares down at you. Glowing red eyes, dark fur covering its body, and claws sharper than knives. Its eyes narrow as it stares at you, looking you up and down as you sit there in fear, unable to move. Its large muzzle moves closer, sniffing the air around you before moving down towards your crotch, sniffing it curiously.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Sad",
                Blush: 2,
                Cry: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ugh…”</span> The creatures makes a noise that is part realization part sigh, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You do not appear to be my normal prey, but you smell like it, child.”</span> You gulp as the creature’s growly voice fills your ear… <span style="Color: BlueViolet">it just talked to you!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You are lucky I have no taste for human flesh, else you would already be devoured.”</span> You are unsure what to do or say, so mumble out something close to a ‘thanks for not eating me’. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Huh…”</span> The creature almost laughs, continuing to sniff the air around you, <span style="Color: Pink">stopping at your hair where it takes several long sniffs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You smell so good though… in other ways…”</span> That’s when you notice it, something familiar between its legs, hard and twitching. Its penis is fully erect, looking almost like a normal human’s though its foreskin seems to be covered in a thin layer of fur. You feel a cold shiver run down your spine as the creature moves in a way to cause its erection to rub against your cheek. The creature shudders at the feeling.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ve never mated with a human child before. It is… tempting. Your scent is so enticing.”</span> The creature moves back to your front, <span style="Color: Yellow">looking at you with hunger in its eyes.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But you are lucky, child, for I have already mated this day. My urges have been satisfied, so you are free to go.”</span> The creature steps back, watching you but giving you space to stand up. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But be warned, child. If you enter these woods again, alone at night, I may not be able to control myself. Your scent is strong and enticing. Even now I can barely contain my desires. Never before have I smelled a human like you, nor one with features of my prey.”</span> The werewolf glances to your ears and tails. <br>
<br>
<div id="choice">
	<<link "Quickly leave<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        Taking your chance and fearing the werewolf may change his mind at any moment, you turn around and run as fast as you can out of the forest. You hear what you imagine is a chuckle along with the something of something following you at a distance, but are too afraid to look back. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Eventually, the sound fades and you find yourself back on the street, safe and sound.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: Yellow">That creature, whatever it really was, probably wasn’t kidding. If you go in there again this late at night, something bad may happen.</span> <br>
        <<set $InActiveQuests.delete("Kitsune: Werewolf")>>
        <<set $CompletedQuests.push("Kitsune: Werewolf")>>
        <<addMoodlet "Feeling Weird" 12>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Wald Street]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Say you might like that<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You smile at the creature, telling it that you may enjoy being bred by it. Your boldness and bravery seem to amuse the creature, as it chuckles at you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You are an interesting one, but be careful what you wish for. My kind is not known for being gentle.”</span> He turns and begins to leave, before adding, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But if you do wish to put your life at risk, return here another day. Your smell will surely entice me, but if it comes to that I cannot guarantee your safety. This was your only warning, child.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        You watch as the creature leaves, enticing yourself by his form. <span style="Color: Yellow">Did you say that just to impress him? Or did you really mean it. Guess the only way to know for sure will be to come back on another night, but is that really a risk you want to take?</span> <br>
        <<set $InActiveQuests.delete("Kitsune: Werewolf")>>
        <<set $CompletedQuests.push("Kitsune: Werewolf")>>
        <<addMoodlet "Feeling Weird" 12>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Wald Street]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>